    "id": "v2-729c1a-p5-practice-slot-2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "The kinetic energy of a moving object is given by $E=\\frac{1}{2}mv^2$ where $E$ is in joules, $m$ is mass in kilograms and $v$ is speed in metres per second.\n\nA cricket ball of mass 160 g has kinetic energy 72 J. Find its speed in km/h.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$v=108\\text{ km/h}$",
      "worked": "$160\\text{ g}=0.16\\text{ kg}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}E&=\\frac{1}{2}mv^2\\\\72&=\\frac{1}{2}(0.16)v^2\\\\72&=0.08v^2\\\\900&=v^2\\\\v&=30\\text{ m/s}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}30\\text{ m/s}&=30\\times3.6\\\\&=108\\text{ km/h}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
